{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1364213-non-artist-dreamers-and-glamour-harvesting","id":1364213,"title":"Non-Artist Dreamers and Glamour Harvesting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-30T13:15:31-08:00","id":1364213,"title":"Non-Artist Dreamers and Glamour Harvesting","content":"The C20 intro says that activists that fight to change corrupt social structures and scientists that want to positively change the world with their research, can touch the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> House Ailils write up says they could gain Dark Glamour from Political intrigues, a Ailils Changling could muse someone like Frank Underwood (from \u2018House of Cards\u2019) to harvest Dark Glamour from their Creative, Machiavellian politics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T17:21:24-08:00","id":1364249,"title":"","content":"Yup.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if there's a question there, but I do like that aspect of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T17:31:26-08:00","id":1364253,"title":"","content":"I know I hope the game showed more of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T23:52:22-08:00","id":1364290,"title":"","content":"Aye, C20 has done a better job then previous editions of saying that anything and everything that inspires passion, motivation, feeling and the like produces glamour.<br /> <br /> Glamour and Dark Glamour are both passion and inspiration. Whether fear that drives people towards better behavior or the inspired passion of a political activist (Glamour) or the terror of a car crash and the dread of a slowly pursuing hunter (Dark Glamour).<br /> <br /> This means that Banality is not, as it's sometimes considered, sadness or misery. There is Glamour in sadness. No, banality is an absence of glamour. It is apathy, malaise, boredom, monotony, and ignorance. Banality is a conscious or subconscious denial of passion. A denial of a person's true joy.<br /> <br /> It's not always totally universal either.<br /> <br /> One person may love to dance and traps glamour from it constantly, but someone who is shy and awkward might not take well to dancing. In fact might even be a banal experience for them because it's a denial of who they are and their true passions, their true will displaced by someone else. If it got bad enough, the embarrassment and frustration could even manifest as Dark Glamour.<br /> <br /> It's an incredibly diverse and unique thing, but I hope this helps folks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T18:45:17-08:00","id":1366202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1364213-non-artist-dreamers-and-glamour-harvesting?p=1364290#post1364290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aye, C20 has done a better job then previous editions of saying that anything and everything that inspires passion, motivation, feeling and the like produces glamour.<br /> <br /> Glamour and Dark Glamour are both passion and inspiration. Whether fear that drives people towards better behavior or the inspired passion of a political activist (Glamour) or the terror of a car crash and the dread of a slowly pursuing hunter (Dark Glamour).<br /> <br /> This means that Banality is not, as it's sometimes considered, sadness or misery. There is Glamour in sadness. No, banality is an absence of glamour. It is apathy, malaise, boredom, monotony, and ignorance. Banality is a conscious or subconscious denial of passion. A denial of a person's true joy.<br /> <br /> It's not always totally universal either.<br /> <br /> One person may love to dance and traps glamour from it constantly, but someone who is shy and awkward might not take well to dancing. In fact might even be a banal experience for them because it's a denial of who they are and their true passions, their true will displaced by someone else. If it got bad enough, the embarrassment and frustration could even manifest as Dark Glamour.<br /> <br /> It's an incredibly diverse and unique thing, but I hope this helps folks.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The clearest example I have is in writing; Poetry makes me zone out like nothing else, boring me to the point of frustration, in almost every case that I've consumed it thus far. It is, to me, a highly banal practice. To my mother, it's her form of self expression. She is a published poet, and nothing inspires her to create more. Its a magic entirely based on perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25663-rigelj","name":"RigelJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T15:42:09-07:00","id":1409969,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s so cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T11:55:24-07:00","id":1410353,"title":"","content":"I am not sure the game properly supports MUSING nonartistic dreamers though or at least I'm having trouble grocking it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T12:36:01-07:00","id":1410366,"title":"","content":"What's needed is creativity; the form it takes doesn't matter so much. <br /> <br /> I find myself thinking of the reason why Martial Arts are called Arts: the people who created them arguably engaged in some creativity. For instance, Bruce Lee hand Jeet Kun Do. Musing involves encouraging creativity in such activities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T15:23:08-07:00","id":1410412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1364213-non-artist-dreamers-and-glamour-harvesting?p=1410366#post1410366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's needed is creativity; the form it takes doesn't matter so much.<br /> <br /> I find myself thinking of the reason why Martial Arts are called Arts: the people who created them arguably engaged in some creativity. For instance, Bruce Lee hand Jeet Kun Do. Musing involves encouraging creativity in such activities.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mean yes and while its thematically good that its easier to ravage.. I can think of really easy ways to Ravage Bruce Lee. I'm having trouble figuring how you inspire him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T00:16:28-07:00","id":1410459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1364213-non-artist-dreamers-and-glamour-harvesting?p=1410412#post1410412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I mean yes and while its thematically good that its easier to ravage.. I can think of really easy ways to Ravage Bruce Lee. I'm having trouble figuring how you inspire him.</div> </div> </div> </div>You inspire him by showing him superhuman feats in a fight and beating him. Superhuman reflexes and agility would be something for a mortal to aspire to achieve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T15:41:39-07:00","id":1410578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1364213-non-artist-dreamers-and-glamour-harvesting?p=1410459#post1410459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You inspire him by showing him superhuman feats in a fight and beating him. Superhuman reflexes and agility would be something for a mortal to aspire to achieve.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But that doesn't inspire him to develop new techniques.. it doesn't even tell me me how i &quot;succeed&quot; What is the base success rate for a Martial artist? How much glamour does someone get from a new punch existing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T17:48:46-07:00","id":1410591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1364213-non-artist-dreamers-and-glamour-harvesting?p=1410412#post1410412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I mean yes and while its thematically good that its easier to ravage.. I can think of really easy ways to Ravage Bruce Lee. I'm having trouble figuring how you inspire him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Inspiring him to find new ways to look at Jeet Kun Do and new techniques to incorporate into it. The footwork, for example, was influenced by both Mohammad Ali's boxing and by Western fencing. But witnessing incredibly talented ballet dancers might also provide further inspiration. Likewise, working out ways to incorporate the philosophy of economy of motion into other actions and arts - such as cooking or flower arraignment - may also inspire new insights. (This is essentially the basis behind the Akashic Brotherhood's use of Do in Mage.)<br /> <br /> As far as non-&quot;art&quot; Glamour, I had always wished 2nd ed had included a book about faith and religion. I always thought a Boggin Wiccan coven leader would be a neat character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T17:55:37-07:00","id":1410593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1364213-non-artist-dreamers-and-glamour-harvesting?p=1410591#post1410591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Inspiring him to find new ways to look at Jeet Kun Do and new techniques to incorporate into it. The footwork, for example, was influenced by both Mohammad Ali's boxing and by Western fencing. But witnessing incredibly talented ballet dancers might also provide further inspiration. Likewise, working out ways to incorporate the philosophy of economy of motion into other actions and arts - such as cooking or flower arraignment - may also inspire new insights. (This is essentially the basis behind the Akashic Brotherhood's use of Do in Mage.)<br /> <br /> As far as non-&quot;art&quot; Glamour, I had always wished 2nd ed had included a book about faith and religion. I always thought a Boggin Wiccan coven leader would be a neat character.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> My problem is the end result. The whole musing mechanic is built around they &quot;make a single awesome thing&quot; rather than a regular stream of bits as they develop their opus. This I think is a problem with Musing in general though. Something that functioned as a bit like reverse ravaging but harder might work better in general as a &quot;you regularly inspire their dreams&quot; rather than big projects since that doesn't work for non artists and even some artists don't quite work. An actor with regular acting work who's inspired couldn't feed glamour for example...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T02:56:59-07:00","id":1410633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1364213-non-artist-dreamers-and-glamour-harvesting?p=1410591#post1410591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Inspiring him to find new ways to look at Jeet Kun Do and new techniques to incorporate into it. The footwork, for example, was influenced by both Mohammad Ali's boxing and by Western fencing. But witnessing incredibly talented ballet dancers might also provide further inspiration. Likewise, working out ways to incorporate the philosophy of economy of motion into other actions and arts - such as cooking or flower arraignment - may also inspire new insights. (This is essentially the basis behind the Akashic Brotherhood's use of Do in Mage.)<br /> <br /> As far as non-&amp;quot;art&amp;quot; Glamour, I had always wished 2nd ed had included a book about faith and religion. I always thought a Boggin Wiccan coven leader would be a neat character.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s mentioned that some members of House Liam can get Glamour from human faith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T05:55:28-07:00","id":1410837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1364213-non-artist-dreamers-and-glamour-harvesting?p=1410593#post1410593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> My problem is the end result. The whole musing mechanic is built around they &quot;make a single awesome thing&quot; rather than a regular stream of bits as they develop their opus. This I think is a problem with Musing in general though. Something that functioned as a bit like reverse ravaging but harder might work better in general as a &quot;you regularly inspire their dreams&quot; rather than big projects since that doesn't work for non artists and even some artists don't quite work. An actor with regular acting work who's inspired couldn't feed glamour for example...</div> </div> </div> </div>A singularly phenomenal duel with a superhuman opponent is the inspiring act. It would be like another finishing a painting.<br /> <br /> And he developed technique rather then techniques. As in he perfected his own physical grace and coordination rather then develop complex moves. Developing Jeet Kune Do was his Magnum Opus, just like another Changeling would Inspire Wagner to compose a lil diddy about magical rings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T15:24:09-07:00","id":1410891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1364213-non-artist-dreamers-and-glamour-harvesting?p=1410837#post1410837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A singularly phenomenal duel with a superhuman opponent is the inspiring act. It would be like another finishing a painting.<br /> <br /> And he developed technique rather then techniques. As in he perfected his own physical grace and coordination rather then develop complex moves. Developing Jeet Kune Do was his Magnum Opus, just like another Changeling would Inspire Wagner to compose a lil diddy about magical rings.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But a changeling would be &quot;better off' by the system having Wagner compose lots of minor works rather than one big thing. LIke someone making jingles is a better dreamer than a great opera.. Bruce lee is even worse you're better off frustrating him breaking him hurting him than inspiring his dream.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T17:19:33-07:00","id":1412354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1364213-non-artist-dreamers-and-glamour-harvesting?p=1410593#post1410593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My problem is the end result. The whole musing mechanic is built around they &quot;make a single awesome thing&quot; rather than a regular stream of bits as they develop their opus. This I think is a problem with Musing in general though. Something that functioned as a bit like reverse ravaging but harder might work better in general as a &quot;you regularly inspire their dreams&quot; rather than big projects since that doesn't work for non artists and even some artists don't quite work. An actor with regular acting work who's inspired couldn't feed glamour for example...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that might be why I want to toss out the &quot;lessened after repeated viewings&quot; thing and just make it you get glamour from the initial viewing of the artwork. So in that case, it's not necessarily a single awesome thing but a good experience. So for the fighter example, watching a single fight would get you the glamour because the fight itself is the art, but you don't need to see him CONSTANTLY invent whole new martial art styles.<br /> <br /> I think revelry may be the key to fixing musing. An Autumn Sidhe, for example, could get revelry from a good inspiring leadership seminar. Or they could get Rapture from their own leadership efforts. Or they may muse a leader and get glamour as that person progresses and succeeds rather than just based on looking at a single finished project.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26403-ragnell","name":"Ragnell","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}